  "methods_and_limits": [
    "Four Current runs follow fixed ABBA order 30/15/15/30 seconds, all with requested onset offset 10 seconds.",
    "Paired deltas are candidate 15s minus adjacent control 30s: slot 2 minus 1, then slot 3 minus 4. Every run remains included.",
    "The 10s phase was selected from the preceding diagnostic; this follow-up does not estimate an unbiased average across all onset phases.",
    "Only the configured reconciliation interval changes; code, binary, Current policy, metrics expression, workload, observer and image identities are checked.",
    "Actual phase comes from observed idle reconciliation timing and is assessed against each assigned 15s or 30s interval with the frozen 2s tolerance.",
    "Observer CPU >55% and controller query timestamps come from separate query calls. Signed observer-to-query gaps are measured observations, not exact causal delay.",
    "Query-start-to-Scale-response and query-return-to-Scale-response are named separately. First successful Scale response uses the actual upward target write.",
    "Ready and Apache request-received timestamps have 1s precision; plots use [t,t+1) bins. Apparent subsecond inversions do not imply negative startup.",
    "Apache server status is not client success. HTTP 200 counts, all-request p95, timeouts and dropped iterations retain the full request population, including drain.",
    "Replica occupancy uses the actual 541s scenario window and 360s post-load tail, integrating 15s replica samples without extrapolating missing coverage.",
    "Reconcile/query counts cover both the whole recorded run and the same actual 541s window. Window/cadence is a reference rate, not an exact expected count; resource events can add reconciliations.",
    "Observer I/O request and round elapsed durations do not quantify CPU overhead or the causal cost of instrumentation.",
    "Frozen analyzer replay validates lineage; the separate independent audit checks calculations without sharing these analyzers.",
    "There are only two runs per cadence at one selected phase. Descriptive paired differences do not establish a global default, superiority, equivalence or production effect."
